OL,3,GNEWSA'Now in a minute' and 'twpsyn'
OL,4,Aadded to Oxford English dictionary
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhat do now in a minute, twpsyn, and
OL,7,Fbwbach have in common?
OL,9,FThey are among six words and phrases
OL,10,Ffrom Wales added to the latest version
OL,11,Fof the Oxford English Dictionary (OED).
OL,13,F"Twpsyn" means fool, and "bwbach" is a
OL,14,Fmischievous creature from Welsh
OL,15,Ffolklore.
OL,17,F"Now in a minute" is used to mean "in a
OL,18,Fmoment", "very soon" or "before long".
